# Next.js, data access, and UI

Specs: `docs/06-api-routes.md` (contract), `docs/14-frontend-architecture.md` (data + state), `docs/09-ui-pages.md` (UI kit + pages).

## Data flow
- UI → hooks (`src/hooks`, TanStack Query) → API library (`src/lib/api`) → transport (fetch `/api/*`, or the mock transport when `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MOCKS=true`).
- Components never call `fetch` or the API library directly; always use a hook. **No server actions** for data.
- DTOs and input schemas come from `src/contracts` only. Don't hand-write response types in components or hooks.
- Buttons come from `allowedActions` on `OfferDTO` / `MilestoneDTO`. Never re-derive role/status rules in components.
- Mutations return the updated `OfferDTO`: `setQueryData(qk.offer(id), offer)`, then invalidate lists, activity, and airwallex-events (plus `qk.wallet` when money settles). Use `qk` from `src/hooks/queryKeys.ts`; no inline key arrays.
- **No optimistic updates for money actions** (pay, approve, cancel, retry).
- Pending states (`offer.isPending` / `milestone.isPending`) use `useOfferSync` (sync every 3s, stop after 60s, expose `timedOut`).

## State
- Server state lives in the Query cache only. Don't copy it into `useState`/context.
- URL state (tabs, method) in `searchParams`; forms via `react-hook-form` + zod resolver with schemas from `src/contracts`; local UI via `useState`.
- No Redux/Zustand. A new global store needs a doc update in `docs/14` first.

## Rendering
- `page.tsx` is a thin server component rendering a client screen from `src/components/screens`. No data fetching in server components.
- Never import `src/lib/airwallex/*`, `src/server/*`, `src/services/*` (except pure `fees.ts`), or Mongoose models into client code.

## Mocks
- Mock handlers (`src/lib/api/mock`) must match the contract and state machines, and use `src/contracts/permissions.ts` and `src/services/fees.ts`. Invalid transitions return 409 `INVALID_STATE`.
- Keep fixtures aligned with `docs/08-seeding.md` personas and offers.

## UI kit
- Primitives in `src/components/ui` (shadcn/ui, restyled with tokens from `docs/09` §2); domain components in `src/components/domain`; status labels/colors only from `src/components/domain/status.ts`.
- Every new component, or new variant or state, is added to `/dev/ui-kit` in the same commit.
- Every data section has loading (skeleton), empty (`EmptyState`), and error (`ErrorState` + retry) states.

## Themes (required)
Spec: `docs/09-ui-pages.md` § Themes. Light and dark both ship. More themes are extra CSS variable sets, not component branches.

- Colours come from semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, status tokens). No hex in components, and no `if (theme === ...)`.
- `dark` is the `dark` class on `<html>` via `next-themes` (`light` | `dark` | `system`, stored as `theme`, default `system`). The `.dark` block must set the same tokens as light, including `--surface`, status colours, and the violet `--primary`.
- A later theme is one registry entry plus a class that redefines those variables. Dark palettes also include the `dark` class.
- Sonner follows the resolved theme. Review new UI in both light and dark on `/dev/ui-kit`.

## Responsiveness (required)
Spec: `docs/09-ui-pages.md` § Responsiveness. Check 375, 768, and 1024+.

- Tailwind mobile-first: default classes are the phone layout; `md` / `lg` add wider layouts. Don't leave a desktop-only layout for later.
- No page-level horizontal scroll. Wide content scrolls inside its own container. Truncating flex children use `min-w-0`. Money stays `whitespace-nowrap`.
- Below `lg`, multi-column pages (create-offer summary, platform balances, UI-kit nav) stack. Sticky side panels are not sticky on small screens.
- Primary actions stay on screen at 375px (pay, approve, submit delivery, send offer). Dialogs are full width with margin below `sm`. Form fields stack below `md`.
- Touch targets are at least 44px tall below `md`.
- Before a screen or component is done, look at it at 375 and 1024, including empty, loading, and error states.

## Checkout
- `@airwallex/components-sdk` only (not `airwallex-payment-elements`). `init({ env: 'demo', enabledElements: ['payments'] })`, mount the Drop-in **before** attaching listeners, and pass only `intent_id`, `client_secret`, and `currency` to the client. In mock mode render `MockCardForm` instead.

## Copy
- "held in escrow" (funded), "released" (approved), "paid" (settled). Always show the fee split. Label payment screens as sandbox/demo. Buttons name outcome and amount.
